adjudication.rationale:
The handler’s auth check is:

```ts
if (req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !== process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET) {
  return res.status(403)
}
```

If `CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is unconfigured (i.e., `process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is `undefined`) and the request does not include that header (so `req.headers[...]` is also `undefined`), the comparison becomes `undefined !== undefined`, which is false, so the request is accepted. Therefore, with credential sharing enabled, the endpoint can be hit without a secret when the env var is missing.
